{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/legendlore/1394739-legendlore-no-ranger-alchemist-and-gunslinger-subclass","id":1394739,"title":"[Legendlore] No Ranger, Alchemist and Gunslinger Subclass?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Legendlore"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-07T02:35:11-07:00","id":1394739,"title":"[Legendlore] No Ranger, Alchemist and Gunslinger Subclass?","content":"Rangers do not specialize in <b>Legendlore</b> setting? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Also, Alchemists and Gunslingers do not have those. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> At least, I do not see those in <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/315126/Legendlore-Manuscript-Preview\" target=\"_blank\">DriveThru Manuscript Preview</a> of game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T23:42:24-07:00","id":1395020,"title":"","content":"Gunslingers have Culverineers, Pistoleers, and Musketeers. Alchemists get Fields of Research, the bomb makers, the mutagen crafters and what have you. And all of the non setting specific specializations for all of the old classes should still be open to your characters. There's no reason a Ranger can't be a beast master in East Azoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T00:30:21-07:00","id":1395025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/partner-worlds/legendlore/1394739-legendlore-no-ranger-alchemist-and-gunslinger-subclass?p=1395020#post1395020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason a Ranger can't be a beast master in East Azoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not remember my D&amp;D 5E - are Ranger subclasses in <b>Players Handbook</b>? Probably yes, as I clearly remember Paladins and Wizards ones from my last read of D&amp;D, few years ago...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-08-2020, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-08T15:02:17-07:00","id":1395159,"title":"","content":"There are subclasses for <i>every</i> class in the Player's Handbook. In the Player's Handbook there are Beast Masters and Hunters, but it seems Hunters were the only ones that went into Open Gaming Content and are listed on the 5th edition SRD. But Rangers do indeed specialize in 5th Edition, the edition is built on having all of these available. And to go further, I'm just saying that I would allow most of the non-setting specific specializations for any class, and even a few of the setting specific ones with details replaced to fit East Azoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}